# The repository is LF — in the index and in the working tree. See docs/DECISIONS.md D95.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect a binary by content, so one added later is left alone.
# `eol=lf` is the half that does the work, and it is NOT redundant with `text=auto`: measured against a
# clone with `core.autocrlf=true`, `text=auto` alone checks out CRLF and this line checks out LF. The
# attribute beats the config — which is the point, since the config is untracked and differs per clone.

* text=auto eol=lf

# The append-only records are UNION-merged: lane branches and the steward add entries to them at once, and
# two entries appended at the same place are both kept rather than conflicting. See docs/DECISIONS.md D214.
# `TASKS.md` is NOT union, because its rows MOVE — a union merge would keep a row in both its old and new
# place. DECISIONS.md's generated index is the one non-appended part: after a merge the steward re-runs
# `decisions-index`, and `decisions-index --check` reports a stale one (it is outside `verify`).

CHANGELOG.md merge=union
docs/DECISIONS.md merge=union
docs/task-archive.md merge=union
docs/FIXES.md merge=union
